<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain</p>
<p>have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to</p>
<p>the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Yoanis	     unloading   wheat	    34,364     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     24,205</p>
<p>Buyukdere	  unloading   barley	    1,305     Europe</p>
<p>Volzky 32	  arrived     fodder wheat    3,174     Europe</p>
<p>Martin Lastis    arrived     corn		2,766     Europe</p>
<p>Seagull	    10/12	 maize grits     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Dnper I	    12/12	 sunflower meal  1,868     Europe</p>
<p>Halilaga	   13/12	 maize, grits    2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Federal Dora     21/12	 barley+	  25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					feed wheat</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	23/12	 wheat+soya     61,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					+corn</p>
<p>Ivonne	     26/12	 corn		4,100     Europe</p>
<p>Fany		 27/12	 corn	     21,733     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya		8,976</p>
<p>				     wheat	     9,081</p>
<p>Unity		30/12	 sorghum	  10,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn	     22,000</p>
<p>				     corn-gluten    11,300</p>
<p>				     corn-screening  6,500</p>
<p>Auk		  02/01	 na		 40,000     U.S.</p>
</text>
